      "body": "### Neovim Version\r\n\r\n0.5.0\r\n\r\n### Operating system/version:\r\n\r\nNixOS 21.05.2486.8ac785da984 (Okapi)\r\n\r\n### Terminal name/version:\r\n\r\nAlacritty 0.8.0\r\n\r\n### TERM environment variable\r\n\r\ntmux-256color\r\n\r\n### Installation\r\n\r\nNix (from nixpkgs-unstable, because 0.5.0 is only in unstable yet)\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nFirst you need to supply Neovim with Perl and `Neovim::Ext` CPAN package (v0.05).\r\n\r\nHere is a minimal reproducible environment for Nix:\r\nhttps://gist.github.com/unclechu/f8d19a4e71a4641c02e5adbbfe064265\r\n1. `nix-build neovim.nix -o neovim`\r\n1. `neovim/bin/nvim` (you can use `-u NORC` if you have some config in your home directory)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n1. Make sure that Perl integration looks totally fine in `:checkhealth`. Should look similar to this:\r\n   \r\n   ``` markdown\r\n   ## Perl provider (optional)\r\n     - INFO: perl executable: /nix/store/wb401ilx27m925s8hi0df79skk5h9rl8-perl-for-neovim/bin/perl\r\n     - OK: Latest \"Neovim::Ext\" cpan module is installed: 0.05\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n1. Run `:perl print \"hi\"` and/or `:perl VIM::Msg(\"hi\")` and see that absolutely nothing happens after you hit Enter. No errors are thrown, nothing. In fact it doesn\u2019t matter what you type after `:perl`, `:perldo`, or `:perlfile`. The result is always the same (nothing happens after execution with no errors in `:msg`).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Vim\r\n\r\nHaven\u2019t checked that, not even sure if Vim has integration with Perl\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nCommands are executed and have effects as in the docs:\r\n- https://neovim.io/doc/user/if_perl.html\r\n- https://neovim.io/doc/user/provider.html#provider-perl\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nAbsolutely nothing happens after execution of `:perl whatever`, `:perldo whatever`, and `:perlfile whatever`. No errors, no effects, nothing.",
